          %h2#ideas_and_objectives Ideas and objectives
          %p
            The motivation of generalized global analytic geometry is to define analytic spaces associated to rig categories, and to use their relations with classical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/global+analytic+geometry"} global analytic spaces
            in order to properly define
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Arakelov+geometry"} Arakelov models
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arithmetic+varieties"} arithmetic varieties
            in an analytic setting.
          %p
            Since rig categories are categorical analogs of associative and commutative semi-rings, a proper theory for them can only be given in the setting of
            = succeed "-categories." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %p
            One will thus need to define
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/overconvergent+global+analytic+geometry"} overconvergent global analytic spaces
            over a given rig
            = succeed "-category," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            = succeed "-topology" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "-topology" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo ⋅
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathbb{R},|\cdot|_\infty)
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo ⋅
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathbb{Z},|\cdot|_\infty)
          %p To be able to complete non-additive rig categories, we will have to replace seminorms by rig metrics (metrics on morphism spaces that are compatible with the rig category structure). There are rig categories associated to rings, but also to Banach rings, and for the last ones, there may be various natural choices, based on the type of modules in use. The notion of morphism will be imposed by the necessity of having a natural morphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Z
                    %mi η
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                  %mo ⋅
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Z
                    %mi η
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                  %mo ⋅
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %mn 2
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi t
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (\Z_\eta,\|\cdot \|_2)\to (\Z_\eta,\|\cdot\|_2)^t
          %p
            for every
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi t
                    %mo ≥
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t\geq 1
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            = succeed "-th" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi t
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi t
                    %mo ∈
                    %msubsup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo +
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t\in \mathbb{R}_+^*
          %h2#seminormed_and_metrized_ring_categories
            Seminormed and metrized ring
            = succeed "-categories" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %p
            A ring
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
            = succeed "-categories." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒜
                  %mo :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mi Rings
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ×
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %mi Cat
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ×
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}:(T_{Rings},\times)\longrightarrow ({}^\infty Cat,\times),
          %p
            we may associate to it a classical ring-category
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi h
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h(\mathcal{A})
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒜
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
            will be a multiplicative seminorm on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi h
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒜
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h(\mathcal{A})
            in the sense of the article cited on this page. If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒜
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
            is a rig category in the classical sense, one may extend it by a kind of nerve construction to a rig
            = succeed "-category." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒜
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N(\mathcal{A})
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒜
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
            gives an
            = succeed "-category." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝔸
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{A}^n
            to
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒜
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N(\mathcal{A})^n
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi N
                    %mrow
                      %mo ⊕
                      %mo ,
                      %mo ⊗
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒜
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi T
                    %mi SRings
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N_{\oplus,\otimes}(\mathcal{A}):T_{SRings}\to {}^\infty Cat
          %p
            given by sending a polynomial map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mi α
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mi α
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝔸
                    %mi n
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi 𝔸
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f=\sum a_\alpha X^\alpha:\mathbb{A}^n\to \mathbb{A}^1
            to the corresponding functor
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi N
                    %mrow
                      %mo ⊕
                      %mo ,
                      %mo ⊗
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi M
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi M
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↦
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⨁
                    %mi α
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊕
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi a
                        %mi α
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi M
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi M
                    %mi n
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi α
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  N_{\oplus,\otimes}(f):=
                  (M_1,\dots,M_n)\mapsto \bigoplus_\alpha\oplus_{a_\alpha}(M_1,\dots,M_n)^{\otimes \alpha}.
          %p
            There is a natural functor from the category of (commutative) rings to the category of ring
            = succeed "-categories" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            to its category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi FMod
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} FMod(A)
            of free finitely generated modules, together with their usual direct sum and tensor product. This functor is fully faithful.
          %p
            Recall that the Berkovich spectrum of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi FMod
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} FMod(\mathbb{Z})
            projects on the space of “Artin” seminorms, that fulfill a weak triangle inequality of the form
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi a
                  %mo +
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo ≤
                  %mi C
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi max
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} |a+b|\leq C\,\max(|a|,|b|).
          %p
            A stable symmetric monoidal
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            = succeed "-category," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            = succeed "-category)." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %p
            One may define the Berkovich spectrum of a ring
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℳ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒜
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi ℳ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi h
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒜
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{M}(\mathcal{A})=\mathcal{M}(h(\mathcal{A})).
          %p
            This means that the Berkovich spectrum doesn’t really encode the homotopy information. However, it is quite practical to work with rig
            = succeed "-categories" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %p We will also work with the notion of a ring metric on a ring category, given by a ring norm on its homotopy category.
          %h2#valuation_rig_categories
            Valuation rig
            = succeed "-categories" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          %p
            Given a multiplicative seminorm
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} |\cdot|
            on a rig
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi O
                    %mi 𝒜
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} O_\mathcal{A}
            whose homotopy category is given by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi h
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi O
                    %mi 𝒜
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi f
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi h
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒜
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo ≤
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h(O_\mathcal{A}):=\{f\in h(\mathcal{A}),\;|f|\leq 1\}.
          %p
            For example, Haran’s definition of the ring of integers of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
            is given by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mi η
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi O
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi FMod
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mo ⋅
                      %msub
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}_\eta:=O_{(FMod(\mathbb{R}),\|\cdot\|_2)}.
          %p
            One may also define an ind-seminormed rig
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mi η
                    %mo †
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} colim
                    %mrow
                      %mi ρ
                      %mo →
                      %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mi O
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi FMod
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mo ⋅
                      %msubsup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mn 2
                        %mi ρ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbb{Z}^\dagger_\eta:=\colim_{\rho\to 1}
                  O_{(FMod(\mathbb{R}),\|\cdot\|^\rho_2)}.
          %p
            Remark that the
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi L
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L^2
            norm
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                  %mo ⋅
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \|\cdot\|_2
            on the rig category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi FMod
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} FMod(\mathbb{R})
            may be extended to a family of norms on the rig category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi FMod
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi X
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mo †
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} FMod(\mathbb{R}\{X\}^\dagger)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℝ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi X
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo †
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathbb{R}\{X\}^\dagger)^n
            the norms given by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mi i
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo ,
                      %mi n
                  %msup
                    %mi X
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %mrow
                      %mi ρ
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 2
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mn ∞
                  %msup
                    %mi ρ
                    %mi i
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo ,
                      %mi n
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mn ∞
                  %msup
                    %mi ρ
                    %mi i
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %mn 2
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\|(\sum a_{i,1} X^i,\dots,\sum a_{i,n} X^i)\|_{\rho,2}:=
                  \\|(\sum |a_{i,1}|_\infty\rho^i,\dots,\sum |a_{i,n}|_\infty\rho^i)\|_2.
          %p
            This seminorm is only sub-multiplicative for the tensor product operation. One may then give a construction of the ind-seminormed rig
            = succeed "-category" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mi η
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi X
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo †
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi O
                    %mrow
                      %mi FMod
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mi X
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mo †
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\mathbb{Z}_\eta\{X\}^\dagger:=O_{FMod(\mathbb{R}\{X\}^\dagger)}.
          %h2#classical_approach_the_metrized_spectrum Classical approach: the metrized spectrum
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒜
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mi 𝒜
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathcal{A},d_{\mathcal{A}})
            is a metrized pointed ring category, we may define its Berkovich spectrum as the set
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo =
                  %mi ℳ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒜
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mi 𝒜
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X=\mathcal{M}(\mathcal{A},d_{\mathcal{A}}(0,\cdot))
            of multiplicative seminorms such that
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo ≤
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi 𝒜
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} |\cdot|\leq d_\mathcal{A}(0,\cdot)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}_x
            at a point
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\in X
            as equivalence classes of pairs
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
