                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}_X
            has a map from rational functions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒦
                    %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{K}_X
            by definition.
          %p Morphisms of analytic spaces will be those induced by morphisms of metrized ring categories.
          %p
            Remark that the point
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi d
                    %mn ∞
                    %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_\infty^\infty
            doesn’t even make sense in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒟
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mi η
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{D}(\mathbb{Z}_\eta,d_\infty)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi d
                    %mn ∞
                    %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_\infty^t(-1,1)
            tends to infinity. However, the associated norm makes sense. Inspired by this remark, we define the rig category of analytic functions on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℳ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi 𝒜
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mi 𝒜
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
